  touches no DOM and knows nothing about forms, so every form you add later depends on the same small surface.

  [34mTracking[39m.[33mgetDeviceId[39m()         [32m// string; generates + persists on first call[39m
  [34mTracking[39m.[33mgetAccountId[39m()        [32m// string | null[39m
  [34mTracking[39m.[33midentify[39m(accountId)   [32m// link this account to this device[39m
  [34mTracking[39m.[33mreset[39m()               [32m// logout: drop the account link, keep the device ID[39m
  [34mTracking[39m.[33mtrack[39m(event, props)   [32m// emit, with both IDs attached automatically[39m

  [38;5;153mtrack()[39m is the seam: today it [38;5;153mconsole.log[39ms a structured object, and swapping in a backend POST or an analytics SDK
  later is a change inside this one function, with no call site touched.

  [1mChanged files:[0m [38;5;153mindex.html[39m gains one [38;5;153m<script src="tracking.js">[39m before the existing [38;5;153mapp.js[39m tag; [38;5;153mapp.js[39m calls into the
  module.

  [1mThe part worth your attention:[0m this design means the [38;5;153muserId[39m parameter you originally asked for doesn't get added. In
  the flow you picked, [38;5;153mlogin()[39m's caller — the submit handler — has no user ID to pass; the device ID lives in the module
  and any account ID only exists [3mafter[0m the server answers. So [38;5;153mlogin()[39m keeps its two parameters and, on success, calls
  [38;5;153mTracking.identify(...)[39m and [38;5;153mTracking.track("login", ...)[39m itself. You get "track who logged in," but via the module
  rather than via the signature. I want that stated plainly rather than buried, since it's a direct departure from the
  literal request.

  The alternative is to add the third parameter anyway — reasonable only if you have an upstream caller I can't see that
  already holds a real user ID.
